'' 'typeof( EXPR )' used as a TYPE outside a declaration -- 'sizeof( typeof( *p ) )' --
'' was parsed as an EXPRESSION: a call to something named 'typeof', which binds to
'' nothing, so the sizeof came out untyped and its statement declined. TypeRef already
'' read the form; only this position never asked it. Measured: 24 for a string ptr
'' deref and 4 for a long one.
''
'' 'type<T>( e )' WHERE T IS NOT A UDT is a CONVERSION and nothing more -- measured,
'' fbc emits 'fb_StrInit( &R$0, -1, &S$0, -1, 0 )' for the string form and
'' 'D$0 = (double)N$0' for the numeric one, which is the same code the bare operand
'' would have produced. The UDT-literal path wants a field list and a UDT to put it in,
'' so every one of these declined.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/typeof-typelit.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/typeof-typelit.out
